                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Live is a satire/comedy platforming game where you advance in levels and interact/fight with various threats/obstacles on the way. You play as a baby in certain parts, as a grown up in others, etc.\n\nThe game is extremely short and honestly, while some aspects of it are rather funny, I can't recommend it in good faith. First of all, the controls and the frame rate are atrocious. This game is also very unfriendly to achievement hunters; I simply forgot to press X during a certain part in the game and I had to exit the game and start a new game which AUTOMATICALLY WIPES YOUR STEAM ACHIEVEMENTS in the process.\n\nI've never seen a game doing this before, but big thumbs down for that, really annoying.\n\nOverall, not really worth the 15-20 minutes for a comedy game, there are less wonky ones out there.",
